// The DEV hostname adapter (#429): a Pages project in the "Shyden Labs Dev"
// account whose custom domains are dev.yawelo-idle.shyden.co.uk,
// dev-api.yawelo-idle.shyden.co.uk and dev-holding.yawelo-idle.shyden.co.uk
// (#768). Every Shyden product's dev lives at
// dev.{product}.shyden.co.uk (operator, 2026-10-06), and that zone is in the
// production account. A Workers Custom Domain must sit in its zone's account,
// while a Pages custom domain needs only a proxied CNAME there, so dev
// reaches its name with no dev credential in production (#395).
//
// Its one Function, functions/[[path]].ts, passes each request on to the
// Worker its host names. Since DEV moved to the non-PROD account (#784,
// Shyden 2026-11-16) that is over HTTPS, at the Worker's workers.dev address
// on ORIGIN_DOMAIN, with the dev door secret (a Pages secret uploaded by the
// deploy): a service binding reaches only its own account's Workers. The
// domains were attached once in the dashboard and are read back by verify-dev
// on every deploy, so the deploy only uploads the Function and its secret.
{
  "$schema": "../../node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "yawelo-idle-dev-hosts",
  // Nothing static: the Function answers every path. The deploy creates the
  // directory empty, because git keeps no empty directory.
  "pages_build_output_dir": "./public",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-10-20",
  "vars": {
    // The non-PROD account's workers.dev domain (#784), read from the account.
    "ORIGIN_DOMAIN": "yawelo-idle-non-prod.workers.dev",
  },
}
